	<section_number>25.1-221</section_number>
	<catch_line>Consolidation of petitions for trial</catch_line>
	<text>
		Unless any party demands a separate hearing on the issue of just compensation, the court may consolidate for trial two or more petitions.
	</text>
	<history>1972, c. 169, § 25-46.17:1; 2003, c. 940.</history>
</law>
